Z||000000||BUhockey||07-17-2001||09:56 AM||||I got this Fiero GT ('88) V6 as a kind of inheritance from my father-in-law .... He always put 5W-30 (I think, I know it was the high grade Mobil1 5W oil) in the car.... but the manual I think says use 10W oil.... which one is better for the engine?!<P>How hot is too hot.... over the weekend my engine was running around 220F.... is that too hot? There is enough coolant in the resevoir ... I checked.... <P>The Fiero is in getting it's 60,000 mile service checkup...<P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero GT V6<P>AOL IM: buhocky13<BR>MSN IM: buhockey13<BR>Yahoo IM: buhockey_13<BR>ICQ: 28847471, 28800545||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||07-17-2001||10:00 AM||||Keep using the Mobil 1 5w30...that stuff will withstand more heat than any regular oil will. It will also form fewer deposits and your engine will run cooler.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||07-17-2001||08:22 PM||||5W-30 or 10W-30 Mobil 1 will work just fine. Mobil1 is way better than any regular oil.<P>210-220 isn't abnormal for an engine. The fact the temp is constant is a good sign.<P>read in my cave to learn more about filling coolant. It would not hurt it to check in back and make sure it's full. The reserve tank isn't always meaningfull. It could have a trapped bubble in back. Probably it's ok but it's worth checking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||07-17-2001||09:13 PM||||Mobil 1 is the way to go (get a Fram 5 Micron Filter to). If you have a manual trans put Mobil 1 in it too, same weight recommended by GM.<P>If you don't mind spending a few dollars to make your car run even better, go to "The Fiero Store" web site and get the performance engine chip, 165 degree thermostat, and related thermal switch. Don't know how strict emissions are in your state, but you can always put the orignal parts back in to meet the test, then swap back. It may even pass with the new parts ?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||formula2||07-17-2001||09:48 PM||||My car does not reach the 125 degree mark..<BR>Good or bad ????<p>[This message has been edited by formula2 (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||formula2||07-18-2001||07:31 AM||||up...||||reg||1
Z||000006||V8Dreamer||07-18-2001||09:37 AM||||deceler, no flames, but from what I've read, 10w30 will form fewer deposits than 5w30 simply because there are fewer polymers in the 10w30....<P>if you know otherwise, please let me know.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000007||hyhy4u||07-18-2001||04:13 PM||||Hey formula2..i got the same problem..except it goes a to about 130-140...cant figure out why it dosnt get any hotter..||||reg||1
Z||000008||johnt671||07-18-2001||05:54 PM||||Either a stuck open thermostst or no thermostat could cause low temps.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||07-18-2001||07:13 PM||||Never trust the dash gauge. hook up and ECM scanner or use something else to get a true reading. <P>Way too many dash gauges have been beat out of calibration from the peg on start bug.||||reg||1
