Z||000013||Tina||07-21-2001||11:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>Never trust the dash gauge. hook up and ECM scanner or use something else to get a true reading. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agree 100%<BR>Happened to me, but with my Autometer-gauge as well.<BR>Ended up driving around with a ray-tec heat gun for a few days.(just point, and measure  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<BR>Wouldn'd recomend buying one (too pricey),but why don't to stop at your local garage after <BR>a little bit of driving and have them measure it.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
